parts.text:
The installed app DOES have the fix! `isNpmCommand`, `ensureSpawnEnv`, and `ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE` are all present. So the fix IS deployed.

But the child process STILL starts the full app. This means our fix of adding `ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1` to `options.env` is NOT working.

Let me think about why. The original exec does:
```js
child = child_process.spawn(command, args, options);
```

Where `options` = `{cwd: installDir, env: {ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE: "1"}}`.

Now, when `child_process.spawn()` is called with `options.env`, the child process should inherit those env vars. Let me test this more carefully:

Actually, wait. The issue might be that when `options.env` is provided to `spawn()`, it COMPLETELY replaces the child's environment instead of merging with the parent's environment. So the child would ONLY have `ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1` but none of the other necessary env vars (PATH, HOME, etc.).

Let me check: `child_process.spawn(command, args, {env: {ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE: "1"}})` would spawn with ONLY that one env var set. The child might not even be able to start properly without PATH, HOME, etc.

Wait, but in my tests earlier, I used:
```js
const env = Object.assign({}, process.env, { ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE: '1' });
```

This merges `process.env` with the new var. But in my `ensureSpawnEnv`:
```js
function ensureSpawnEnv(options) {
    const opts = Object.assign({}, options);
    const env = Object.assign({}, (options && options.env) || {});
    env.ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE = "1";
    opts.env = env;
    return opts;
}
```

This creates `env` from `options.env` which is `undefined` (since the original options only have `cwd`). So `env = Object.assign({}, undefined || {})` = `{}`. Then `env.ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE = "1"` makes it `{ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE: "1"}`. This replaces the child's env entirely!

I need to include `process.env` in the merge:
```js
const env = Object.assign({}, process.env, (options && options.env) || {});
env.ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE = "1";
opts.env = env;
```

This way, the child inherits the parent's full environment plus `ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1`.

That's the bug! The `ensureSpawnEnv` function was missing `process.env` in the merge.

